{"name":"Matisse","hex":"#365c7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Matisse (Mexican band)","blocks":[{"text":"Matisse is a Mexican pop band formed in 2014 in Mexicali, composed of Melissa Robles, Pablo Preciado, and Román Torres. Their discography includes the studio albums Sube (2015), Por tu bien (2017), Tres (2020), Así de Enamorados (2020), De norte a sur (2022), and Bella Nostalgia (2024)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Matisse2025.jpg/330px-Matisse2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matisse_(Mexican_band)","wikidata":"Q30919091"},{"title":"Matisse (Greek band)","blocks":[{"text":"Matisse is an English language-singing alternative rock band from Athens, Greece formed in 1999. They took their name from the famous French painter Henri Matisse."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matisse_(Greek_band)","wikidata":"Q6787601"},{"title":"Henri Matisse","blocks":[{"text":"Henri Émile Benoît Matisse was a French visual artist, known for both his use of colour and his fluid and original draughtsmanship. He was a draughtsman, printmaker, and sculptor, but is known primarily as a painter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Henri_Matisse%2C_1913%2C_photograph_by_Alvin_Langdon_Coburn.jpg/330px-Henri_Matisse%2C_1913%2C_photograph_by_Alvin_Langdon_Coburn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Matisse","wikidata":"Q5589"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Reading_henri_matisse.jpg/500px-Reading_henri_matisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Reading_henri_matisse.jpg/500px-Reading_henri_matisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum